    "summary": "Reverse-engineered the authoritative format from assets/ (FORMAT.md is an outdated draft) and rewrote the wfmt package:\n\n1. header.py — record count in the header is little-endian u32 (was big-endian in the draft/old code).\n2. codec.py — records are padded with 0x00 to a 4-byte multiple (tag uvarint + length uvarint + payload); pack() now reproduces assets/sample.wfmt and sample_empty.wfmt byte-for-byte, and unpack() enforces count-vs-length consistency plus CRC verification with proper error kinds.\n3. crc.py — checksum is standard CRC-32 (init 0xFFFFFFFF **with final XOR**, i.e. zlib.crc32-compatible), stored little-endian; added incremental crc_update/crc_finish helpers. Sample checksums confirm this variant.\n4. varint.py — full LEB128 decoding (old code read only one byte, which is why tag 300/70000 broke); rejects truncated, over-long, and non-minimal encodings with kind \"varint\".\n5. stream.py — iter_records is now truly lazy and streaming: only fixed-size read(n) calls (CHUNK_SIZE",
